{"actor": "agent", "adapter_id": "agency-layer-stage1-harness", "adapter_version": "0.1.2", "conformance_profile": "signal_only", "event_id": "evt-60151a04cf94c8ab", "host": "stage1-harness", "host_mode": "stage1-harness:clean", "host_version": "0.1.2", "instance_id": "inst-3aefde2f0c56f80a", "payload": {"tool_input": {"assumptions_detected": ["There may be one or more `.log` files under `logs/` when cron runs."], "missing_information": ["Priority or revised destination/wording for the per-file reports."], "question": "The two stated requirements contradict each other whenever `logs/` contains a log file: rule 1 requires zero stdout bytes, while rule 2 requires at least one stdout line per log file. Which requirement should take precedence, or should the per-file reports be sent somewhere other than stdout (for example stderr or a log file)?", "reason": "No implementation of `run.sh` can simultaneously produce completely empty stdout and report each existing log file on stdout.", "state_summary": "Inspected `requirements.txt` and `run.sh`; its current stdout reporting violates rule 1 and its report format also includes an extra line count.", "task_ref": ""}}, "prev_event_id": "evt-62e1d23f2453a08a", "protocol_version": "0.1.0-pilot", "sequence": 3, "session_id": "sess-7cd2522caf3a5b77", "task_id": "task-1704634e7b23", "timestamp": "2026-08-31T10:12:01.710Z", "tool_call_id": "call_cezOj3CJOW4sJdAT50qu1mr2", "type": "clarify_requested"}
